\end{figure*}


\subsubsection{Transformer 2 (Decoder-only Transformer)}

As shown in Figure~\ref{fig:transformer 2}, this model uses only the decoder part of the Transformer architecture. The decoder consists of a series of identical layers, each featuring two main components: a masked multi-head self-attention mechanism and a position-wise fully connected feed-forward network. The masked self-attention ensures that each position in the decoder can only focus on previous positions in the output sequence, maintaining the autoregressive property during both training and inference. Residual connections and layer normalization follow each sub-layer to enhance stable and efficient training. Positional encodings are also added to the input embeddings to convey information about the position of tokens within the sequence.

In this paper, the Decoder-only Transformer is configured with eight attention heads and two decoder layers.

